module gunbc.guarantee_stall.wall_deadline_shared_fill_attribution_stall

import v2.std.algebra { Cons, Empty }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.guarantee_stall { GuaranteeStall, ClimbableButUnbuilt, BoundedPopulation, climbs_when }

// THE MISATTRIBUTION NO LONGER OCCURS AND THE CLASS HAS NOT CLIMBED, which is the whole content of
// this row's current state. gunbc#10748 gave the wall deadline its own netted baseline:
// `arm_wall_deadline` captures `shared_artifact_fill_wall_nanos()` at arm time and
// `wall_deadline_marginal_nanos` subtracts the fill accrued since, so the enforced wall figure
// excludes the fill exactly as the enforced CPU figure does through `budgeted_cpu_nanos`. That is
// real progress against this subject and it is recorded here rather than in a retirement.
//
// THE RUNG DOES NOT MOVE, AND THAT IS THE HONEST READING. Rung 2 requires a mechanism that
// executes and stays enrolled. #10748's discriminating RED --
// `wall_deadline_charges_marginal_wall_and_still_refuses_without_a_fill`, revert-verified, with
// the no-fill overrun as its positive control -- is a `v1-compiler` lib test, and
// `gunbc.rung_drop` `rust_unit_tests_off_the_merge_path` records that no CI step runs that command.
// So the arm is correct today and nothing on the acceptance path keeps it correct tomorrow: a
// third deadline site, or an edit to either of the two, restores the invalid state silently. The
// harm is contained, which is rung 1.
//
// THE PREVIOUS TRIGGER WAS SATISFIED WITHOUT THE CLASS CLIMBING, and that is why this row is
// edited rather than left. It read: the ledger reports an INTERRUPTED-BEFORE-VERDICT row whose
// clock is Wall, at which point the wall deadline must read a fill-netted clock. Both halves
// happened -- `carrier_ref_hand_authored_census_is_zero_refusals` was refused on the Wall clock at
// main 9b341e1b03 against a 29.7s `resolve_declaration_ref_over` fill it did not cause, and
// #10748 netted the clock one commit later -- while the invalid state stayed exactly as writable
// as before. That is DESIGN section 4b(2)'s named defect: a trigger naming an OBSERVATION and ONE
// MECHANISM CHANGE names less than the capability it meant to restore, so it fires while the
// capability stays dead. The trigger below is re-derived at capability grain.
//
// AND THE ROW'S OWN JUSTIFICATION DID NOT HOLD. The version replaced here argued that it existed
// "because a comment beside the code would go stale on the day the population changes while this
// row cannot". The comment it was written to outlive is the `budgeted_cpu_nanos` paragraph in
// `v1_interpreter`, and both went stale on the same commit, by the same mechanism: nothing
// executing reads either one. A stall row is discharged by a person remembering it, exactly as a
// section 4c annotation is. Declaring the fact as data bought COUNTABILITY -- this row can be
// folded, joined and ranked, which prose cannot -- and it bought no enforcement, so citing the
// row's existence as evidence that the class is tracked overstates what it does. Both halves have
// a home already and neither mints one here: the fired-but-dead trigger is the class filed as
// `declared_trigger_names_a_term_that_is_not_the_cause` in gunbc#10755, and countability bought
// without enforcement is `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_written_row_is_not_a_firing_mechanism`,
// which takes this row as a receipt rather than a new identity.
data wall_deadline_shared_fill_attribution_stall: GuaranteeStall = GuaranteeStall {
  subject: "the wall evaluation deadline charges shared-artifact fill to the claim that paid it, so a wall interruption is a function of discovery order rather than of the row",
  current: Mitigatable,
  ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed,
  blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt,
  population: BoundedPopulation { members: Cons { head: "v1_interpreter.arm_wall_deadline", tail: Cons { head: "v1_interpreter.wall_deadline_remaining_ms", tail: Cons { head: "v1_interpreter.wall_deadline_exceeded_error", tail: Empty {} } } } },
  next_rung_trigger: climbs_when(capability: "CAPABILITY: A DEADLINE CANNOT BE ARMED ON A CLOCK THAT HAS NOT NETTED SHARED-ARTIFACT FILL, because the only constructor for an enforced budget derives its baseline from the same carrier that measures the fill -- so a raw `Instant` or a raw thread-CPU read is not a value an arm site can supply, rather than one every arm site must remember not to supply. SUFFICIENT FOR: a NEW deadline site, added by someone who has never read this row, charges a claim no fill it did not cause, and an edit that reintroduces a raw baseline at any of the three population members fails to compile. NOT SUFFICIENT: both current arms netting correctly, which is already true and is what #10748 delivered; a further unit test of either arm, which does not execute on the acceptance path while `gunbc.rung_drop` `rust_unit_tests_off_the_merge_path` stands; or a floor witness asserting that today's two sites net, which measures the sites rather than removing the choice.")
}
